    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d879">

                <pb facs="0704" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12945, 12949.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Silliman to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Carranza made a triumphal entry into the capital this morning. The Plaza
                    de Armas was thronged with many thousands. He spoke from one of the balconies of
                    the National Palace. Tremendous ovation and no disorder whatever. The only
                    representative of the local Diplomatic Corps present was the French Chargé
                    d’Affaires. In his speech Carranza made appreciative reference to the
                    Administration’s Mexican policy.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
